did not depend on OCR/text-extraction of the source PDF — the paper
was read directly by the replicating agent and the transpiler pipeline
was implemented against the paper's mathematical statements + Qiskit
0.22-era `rzx_templates` and `RZXCalibrationBuilder` reference code.

## Headline content extracted by hand (verified against PDF)

- **Method:** Expose $R_{ZX}(\theta)$ as a native continuous-angle
  two-qubit gate whose calibrated pulse is obtained by linearly
  scaling the pulse area of the already-calibrated
  $\mathrm{CX}=R_{ZX}(\pi/2)$. Insert a template-substitution pass
  that rewrites $\mathrm{CX}\text{-}R_z(\theta)\text{-}\mathrm{CX}$
  ($=R_{ZZ}(\theta)$) and related two-qubit blocks into echoed pairs
  of scaled $R_{ZX}(\theta/2)$ pulses.

- **Quantitative headline 1:** Up to ~50 % process-error reduction
  for $R_{ZZ}(\theta)$ and arbitrary SU(4) gates measured by process
  tomography on IBM Q hardware (Fig. 4 region).

- **Quantitative headline 2:** For depth-1 QAOA MAX-CUT on an
  11-node non-native graph on `ibmq_mumbai`: 42–52 % schedule-time
  reduction; max avg-cut deviation $3.65 \to 2.26$ (38 % reduction).

- **Coherence-limited noise model (App. C):** Per-gate depolarising
  rate is linear in pulse duration; used as the reference model in
  this replication.

